{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"tar -xOf logic2b-mcp-0.2.0.tgz package/README.md\ntar -xOf logic2b-mcp-0.2.0.tgz package/dist/index.js | rg -n -C 4 'scaffold_plan|preset|benchmark' | sed -n '1,240p'\"","aggregated_output":"# @logic2b/mcp\n\nAn [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) server that exposes the\n[logic2b ui](https://ui.logic2b.com) registry to coding agents. Point your\nagent at it and it can discover, read, theme and **install** every component,\nblock and chart — without leaving the conversation and without a shell.\n\n## Tools\n\n### Read the registry\n\n| Tool | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `list_components` | List registry items. Filter by `kind` (`component` \\| `block` \\| `chart` \\| `theme`) or `category`. |\n| `search_components` | Keyword search ranked by name/title/description, e.g. `\"login form\"`, `\"donut chart\"`. |\n| `get_component` | Fetch an item's full payload by `name`: dependencies, registry dependencies and the complete source of every file. |\n| `get_demo` | Usage examples for an item — the demo components the docs render, with imports rewritten to installed-project paths. |\n\n### Act on a project\n\n| Tool | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `install_plan` | Resolve items into an executable plan: every file to write (project-relative path + full content, registry dependencies resolved) and the npm dependencies to add. No command to run — write the files, add the deps, done. |\n| `add_command` | The exact `logic2b add` invocation (npm/pnpm/yarn/bun, names validated) for when a shell **is** available. |\n| `get_theme` | The theme.css stylesheet, its npm deps, and the customization catalog (base scales, accents, chart palettes, radii, fonts). |\n| `decode_preset` | Decode a `/create` preset id into its config and the exact token values it pins for light and dark. |\n| `apply_preset` | Build a themed theme.css from a preset id or explicit choices; optionally patch a stylesheet you pass in. Returns the CSS and the canonical preset id. |\n| `contrast_audit` | WCAG 2.2 + APCA contrast of every text token pair (light + dark) for a preset, explicit options or raw token values — verify a generated theme before shipping it. |\n\n`get_component` returns exactly what `npx logic2b add <name>` installs;\n`install_plan` turns that into file writes an agent can execute directly.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Remote endpoint (zero install)\n\nThe same tools are served over streamable HTTP at\n`https://ui.logic2b.com/mcp` — nothing to run locally, which also works for\nweb-based assistants and sandboxed agents without a shell. With Claude Code:\n\n```bash\nclaude mcp add --transport http logic2b https://ui.logic2b.com/mcp\n```\n\nOr in any client that takes a JSON config:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"logic2b\": { \"type\": \"http\", \"url\": \"https://ui.logic2b.com/mcp\" }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Local (stdio)\n\nThe server speaks stdio and needs no configuration. Add it to any MCP client.\n\n**Claude Desktop / Claude Code** (`claude_desktop_config.json` or `.mcp.json`):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"logic2b\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@logic2b/mcp\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Cursor** (`.cursor/mcp.json`) uses the same shape.\n\n### Pointing at a different registry\n\nBy default the server reads from `https://ui.logic2b.com`. Override it with the\n`LOGIC2B_REGISTRY` environment variable (useful for a self-hosted registry):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"logic2b\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@logic2b/mcp\"],\n      \"env\": { \"LOGIC2B_REGISTRY\": \"https://ui.example.com\" }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Development\n\n```bash\npnpm --dir packages/mcp dev     # run from source (tsx)\npnpm --dir packages/mcp test    # unit tests (node:test)\npnpm --dir packages/mcp build   # emit dist/\n```\n\n## License\n\nMIT © [logic2b](https://ui.logic2b.com)\n728-    \"sidebar-border\": tokens.border,\n729-    \"sidebar-ring\": tokens.ring\n730-  };\n731-}\n732:function presetDeclarations(cfg, mode) {\n733-  const { tokens, chart } = resolveTokens(cfg, mode);\n734-  const decls = { ...tokens };\n735-  chart.forEach((c, i) => decls[`chart-${i + 1}`] = c);\n736-  Object.assign(decls, sidebarTokens(cfg, mode));\n--\n760-${missing.join(\"\\n\")}`;\n761-  return css.slice(0, start) + block + css.slice(end);\n762-}\n763-function applyPresetToCss(css, cfg) {\n764:  let out = patchBlock(css, \":root\", presetDeclarations(cfg, \"light\"));\n765:  out = patchBlock(out, \".dark\", presetDeclarations(cfg, \"dark\"));\n766-  return out;\n767-}\n768-\n769-// src/tools.ts\n--\n869-    }\n870-  },\n871-  {\n872-    name: \"get_theme\",\n873:    description: \"Fetch the logic2b theme: the theme.css stylesheet (every design token the components consume), its npm dependencies, and the customization catalog \\u2014 available base scales, accents, chart palettes, radii and fonts plus the defaults. Use it to install the design system or to see what apply_preset can change.\",\n874-    inputSchema: { type: \"object\", properties: {} }\n875-  },\n876-  {\n877:    name: \"decode_preset\",\n878:    description: \"Decode a theme preset id from the /create studio (or from apply_preset) into its configuration and the exact CSS custom-property values it pins for light and dark mode. Use it to inspect or verify a theme without applying it.\",\n879-    inputSchema: {\n880-      type: \"object\",\n881-      properties: {\n882:        preset: {\n883-          type: \"string\",\n884:          description: \"The preset id, e.g. from a /create share link or DESIGN.md.\"\n885-        }\n886-      },\n887:      required: [\"preset\"]\n888-    }\n889-  },\n890-  {\n891:    name: \"apply_preset\",\n892:    description: \"Build a themed theme.css: takes a preset id (or explicit choices \\u2014 base scale, accent, chart palette, radius, fonts) and returns the theme stylesheet with those exact token values patched in, ready to write into the project, plus the canonical preset id. Pass your project's current theme.css as `css` to re-theme an existing install without losing local edits outside the token blocks.\",\n893-    inputSchema: {\n894-      type: \"object\",\n895-      properties: {\n896:        preset: {\n897-          type: \"string\",\n898:          description: \"A preset id from /create. Omit it to compose a theme from the explicit options below.\"\n899-        },\n900-        base: { type: \"string\", description: 'Base gray scale: \"neutral\", \"stone\", \"zinc\", \"slate\" or \"gray\".' },\n901-        accent: { type: \"string\", description: 'Accent color: \"base\" (monochrome), \"blue\", \"green\", \"rose\", \"violet\", \"orange\" \\u2014 or a custom oklch hue/chroma as \"h<hue>c<chroma>\" (hue 0-360, chroma 0-0.4), e.g. \"h250c0.2\". Text color is picked by contrast automatically.' },\n902-        chart: { type: \"string\", description: 'Chart palette: \"default\", \"blue\", \"green\", \"violet\", \"rose\", \"orange\" \\u2014 or a custom \"h<hue>c<chroma>\" ramp.' },\n--\n911-    }\n912-  },\n913-  {\n914-    name: \"contrast_audit\",\n915:    description: \"Audit a theme's text contrast: WCAG 2.2 ratios and APCA Lc values for every foreground/background token pair, light and dark mode. Takes a preset id or explicit theme options (same as apply_preset), or raw token values via `tokens`. A pair warns when it misses WCAG AA (4.5:1) or |Lc| 60. Use it to verify a theme you generated before shipping it.\",\n916-    inputSchema: {\n917-      type: \"object\",\n918-      properties: {\n919:        preset: { type: \"string\", description: \"A /create preset id to audit.\" },\n920:        base: { type: \"string\", description: \"Base gray scale (see apply_preset).\" },\n921:        accent: { type: \"string\", description: \"Accent color (see apply_preset).\" },\n922:        chart: { type: \"string\", description: \"Chart palette (see apply_preset).\" },\n923-        radius: { type: \"string\", description: \"Corner radius (ignored by the audit).\" },\n924-        font: { type: \"string\", description: \"Body font (ignored by the audit).\" },\n925-        heading: { type: \"string\", description: \"Heading font (ignored by the audit).\" },\n926-        tokens: {\n927-          type: \"object\",\n928:          description: 'Optional raw token map ({\"primary\": \"oklch(\\u2026)\", \"primary-foreground\": \"oklch(\\u2026)\", \\u2026}) to audit instead of a preset \\u2014 audits just these values as one mode.'\n929-        }\n930-      }\n931-    }\n932-  }\n--\n951-    isError: true\n952-  };\n953-}\n954-function resolveThemeArgs(args) {\n955:  const preset = typeof args.preset === \"string\" ? args.preset.trim() : \"\";\n956:  if (preset) {\n957:    const cfg2 = decodePreset(preset);\n958:    return cfg2 ?? `\"${preset}\" is not a valid preset id.`;\n959-  }\n960-  const tables = [\n961-    [\"base\", \"base\", BASE_COLORS],\n962-    [\"theme\", \"accent\", ACCENTS],\n--\n1056-          yarn: `yarn dlx logic2b@latest add ${names}`,\n1057-          bun: `bunx logic2b@latest add ${names}`\n1058-        },\n1059-        notes: [\n1060:          \"If the project has no components.json yet, run `npx logic2b@latest init` first (add --preset <id> to apply a /create theme).\",\n1061-          \"The command resolves registry dependencies and prints the npm packages to install.\",\n1062-          \"No shell available? Use the install_plan tool instead \\u2014 it returns the file writes directly.\"\n1063-        ]\n1064-      });\n--\n1090-          radius: RADII,\n1091-          font: FONTS\n1092-        },\n1093-        notes: [\n1094:          \"Every option combination is addressable as a preset id \\u2014 use apply_preset to get the patched stylesheet, decode_preset to inspect one.\",\n1095:          'The config key for the accent is \"theme\" (historical); the apply_preset argument is \"accent\".',\n1096-          'Beyond the named accents/charts, any oklch hue/chroma works as a custom key: \"h<hue>c<chroma>\" (hue 0-360, chroma 0-0.4), e.g. accent \"h250c0.2\". The readable text color is derived by contrast.'\n1097-        ]\n1098-      });\n1099-    }\n1100:    if (name === \"decode_preset\") {\n1101:      const preset = String(args.preset ?? \"\").trim();\n1102:      if (!preset) return errorResult('The \"preset\" argument is required.');\n1103:      const cfg = decodePreset(preset);\n1104-      if (!cfg) {\n1105-        return errorResult(\n1106:          `\"${preset}\" is not a valid preset id (expected base64url of \"base|accent|chart|radius|font|heading\" with known values).`\n1107-        );\n1108-      }\n1109-      return textResult({\n1110:        preset,\n1111-        config: cfg,\n1112-        declarations: {\n1113:          light: presetDeclarations(cfg, \"light\"),\n1114:          dark: presetDeclarations(cfg, \"dark\")\n1115-        }\n1116-      });\n1117-    }\n1118:    if (name === \"apply_preset\") {\n1119-      const cfg = resolveThemeArgs(args);\n1120-      if (typeof cfg === \"string\") return errorResult(cfg);\n1121-      let css = typeof args.css === \"string\" && args.css.trim() ? args.css : void 0;\n1122-      let npmDependencies;\n--\n1127-      }\n1128-      const patched = applyPresetToCss(css, cfg);\n1129-      return textResult({\n1130-        registry: base,\n1131:        preset: encodePreset(cfg),\n1132-        config: cfg,\n1133-        file: { path: \"src/styles/theme.css\", content: patched },\n1134-        ...npmDependencies ? { npmDependencies } : {},\n1135-        notes: [\n1136-          \"Write the file into the project (or overwrite the existing theme.css) \\u2014 only the token values inside :root and .dark change.\",\n1137:          \"Reproduce this exact theme anywhere with `npx logic2b@latest init --preset <preset>` or the /create studio.\"\n1138-        ]\n1139-      });\n1140-    }\n1141-    if (name === \"contrast_audit\") {\n--\n1147-        });\n1148-      }\n1149-      const cfg = resolveThemeArgs(args);\n1150-      if (typeof cfg === \"string\") return errorResult(cfg);\n1151:      const light = auditTokens(presetDeclarations(cfg, \"light\"));\n1152:      const dark = auditTokens(presetDeclarations(cfg, \"dark\"));\n1153-      const warnings = [...light, ...dark].filter((r) => r.warn);\n1154-      return textResult({\n1155:        preset: encodePreset(cfg),\n1156-        config: cfg,\n1157-        thresholds: { wcag: \"AA 4.5:1 for body text\", apca: \"|Lc| \\u2265 60\" },\n1158-        light,\n1159-        dark,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
